{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"079f8ea6dfd37566976ad1ecd503be92294b9a7b743779e5449c0fe85ee79f41","digest":{"component_or_area":"grounding/engine_b_backends.py — OpenGrep validation deduplication","key_entities":["_run_opengrep","engine_b_backends.py","semgrep --validate","source_path","test_opengrep_validation_runs_once_per_source_file","test_opengrep_shared_source_validation_failure_fans_out_to_every_detector","test_engine_b.py","test_conformance.py","test_coverage_reconstruction.py"],"problem_keywords":["validation deduplication","opengrep configuration","call-local caching","semgrep validator","detector source file reuse","test boundary preservation"],"propositions":["Within a single _run_opengrep invocation, semgrep --validate --config must execute exactly once per unique detector source_path, with the validation result fanned out to all detectors declared from that source.","A shared-source validation failure must quarantine every detector from that source as invalid_detector while preserving per-detector detail and allowing other good detectors to continue scanning.","The validation cache must be call-local only (a dict keyed by source_path inside _run_opengrep); no module-level, persistent, or cross-scan state is introduced.","Scan execution, SARIF normalization, coverage records, and all existing analyzer boundary tests remain unchanged; no scanner invocation is removed or mocked in production code."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787687153098593001,"uuid":"a07300b4-1d68-41b7-be4e-d5544009e896"}